# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The About box, in the R5 manner: reached from the Deskbar and from the
# global bar's system menu, modeless, closed by Escape -- and its facts
# come from the host underneath, not from constants.
wait 12
note from the Deskbar first, whose About row had no consumer until now
press 900 20 1
wait 2
release 900 20 1
wait 4
menu-pick About this system
wait 6
expect-title About this system
note Escape closes it, as a panel that announces should
key Escape
wait 4
expect-no-title About this system
note and CLOSED means closed, not defocused: the title noun reads the
note FOCUSED window, so it alone cannot tell a closed panel from one that
note lost focus -- the spot where the amber rule stood shows the folder
note window's own paper again only when the panel is really gone
expect-pixel 330 290 ffffff
note and from the global bar's Tiku menu, the corner ritual's first row
write /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings GlobalMenuBar on
wait 20
click 20 8
wait 4
expect-menu About this system
note and the strip's About row wears the same mark the leaf's does, from
note the same geometry -- so the two ways in to the box look like one thing
expect-pixel 22 31 f7e689
menu-pick About this system
wait 6
expect-title About this system
note the identity column wears the wordmark over its amber rule
note the accent rule sits under the wordmark, which sits under the MARK,
note and is eighty pixels lower than it was for exactly that reason -- so
note this pins the mark's presence without pinning its COLOUR, which
note cycles: a pixel of the logo itself would pass or fail by the clock
expect-pixel 330 290 ffcb00
note the wordmark over that rule is the product's name, not the first
note four letters of it -- pinned on the upright of the O, which is ten
note pixels further right than "Tiku" ever reached
expect-pixel 351 276 000000
note the facts beside it are the release and then only what the machine
note can answer for itself.  The release line is pinned on a stroke of
note "TikuDesktop" rather than on the number, so a version can be raised
note without editing a test
expect-pixel 496 185 000000
note and the memory gauge is pinned on the top edge of its frame, which
note is where it is only because the column has exactly the lines it has:
note put a build date or a kernel string back above it and the gauge
note moves down and this fails, which is the point of pinning a RULE and
note not a glyph -- the bar's fill depends on the host, its frame does not
expect-pixel 670 249 828282
note and the footer says three things now: whose it is, where the project
note lives, and on what terms.  A script cannot read a string, so the page
note and the licence are each pinned on a stroke of their own text -- the
note crossbars of "http" for one, an upright of the licence line for the
note other -- which also pins that the box grew the line to put them on
expect-pixel 499 324 000000
expect-pixel 419 345 000000
quit
